{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"An Irish UCITS ManCo must appoint delegates only where they are suitably qualified and capable, with adequate resources, sound procedures and controls, and (for investment managers) appropriate authorisation and good repute. It must conduct due diligence, assess conflicts, define the mandate and reporting arrangements in a written agreement, and ensure delegation does not impair effective supervision or prevent the ManCo from acting in investors’ best interests.\n\nAfter appointment, it must continuously monitor performance and compliance, obtain and review regular reports, assess financial and operational capability, manage conflicts, and take corrective action—including termination—where needed. Oversight must be proportionate to the delegate’s role and risks; delegation cannot become “letter-box” management.\n\nThe ManCo remains fully responsible to the UCITS and its investors for its obligations, notwithstanding delegation."}}
